[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (4.8,0) node[midway,below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4.8,0) -- (4.8,2) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (4.8,2) -- (0,2) -- cycle;
\node[above] at (2.4,2) {$A$};
\draw (6,0) -- (10,0) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (10,0) -- (10,2.4) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (10,2.4) -- (6,2.4) -- cycle;
\node[above] at (8,2.4) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The rectangles have equal area.
Which has the smaller perimeter, and by how much?
